## Phase 1: Database Migration (Priority: HIGH)

### 1.1 Create Migration Script

**File**: `C:\Users\31936\Desktop\AgentMemory\database\migration_add_deleted_fields.sql`

```sql
-- Migration: Add deleted field to user_profiles, project_contexts, skills
-- Date: 2026-03-22
-- Author: System Migration

BEGIN;

-- Add deleted column to user_profiles
ALTER TABLE user_profiles 
ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;

-- Add deleted column to project_contexts
ALTER TABLE project_contexts 
ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;

-- Add deleted column to skills
ALTER TABLE skills 
ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;

-- Create indexes for deleted filtering
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_user_profiles_deleted ON user_profiles(deleted);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_project_contexts_deleted ON project_contexts(deleted);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_skills_deleted ON skills(deleted);

-- Add comments for documentation
COMMENT ON COLUMN user_profiles.deleted IS 'Soft delete flag (true = deleted)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project_contexts.deleted IS 'Soft delete flag (true = deleted)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN skills.deleted IS 'Soft delete flag (true = deleted)';

COMMIT;

-- Verification queries (run these to verify migration)
-- SELECT COUNT(*) as user_profiles_count FROM user_profiles WHERE deleted IS NULL;
-- SELECT COUNT(*) as project_contexts_count FROM project_contexts WHERE deleted IS NULL;
-- SELECT COUNT(*) as skills_count FROM skills WHERE deleted IS NULL;
```

**Migration Strategy**:
- Use `IF NOT EXISTS` for safety (can run multiple times)
- Default existing records to `deleted = false` (not deleted)
- Create indexes for performance on `WHERE deleted = false` queries
- Wrap in transaction for atomicity

